From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:45:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: early_signal: signal finished submissions
 before admission

The pump retired, then admitted and published up to 64 Works and rang
the doorbell, and only then signalled one finished submission per pass.
With K finished submissions the K-th fence waited behind K admission
passes: retire-seen to fence signal p50 229 us, p90 694 us in Dota
(claude-tl-fw158). Signal every finished submission right after the
retire scan, with the locks dropped, then admit. Upstream likewise
signals completions from its event path. early_signal=0 (boot or debugfs
asahi_m4/early_signal) restores the old order for A/B.

Folded in:
- WIP drm/asahi: G16 signal finished submissions before each admission pass
- WIP drm/asahi: G16 early_signal=2 (publish, then batch-signal); no per-scan allocation

[WIP drm/asahi: G16 early_signal=2 (publish, then batch-signal); no per-scan allocation]
#161's code costs ~4.6% fps in default-mode Dota (bracket vs #149,
timeline off). Two suspects get alternatives:
- early_signal=2 keeps #149's order, admission and doorbell first, so
  an idle GPU gets the next Work without waiting for fence callbacks,
  then signals every finished submission in one batch with the locks
  dropped instead of one per pump pass. 1 (default) and 0 unchanged;
  all three switch at runtime through debugfs asahi_m4/early_signal.
- The retire word snapshot uses a fixed 32-entry stack table instead
  of a KVec allocated per scan; words past it are read directly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
